From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: tolerate a rejected extended features page above 1

The MediaTek MT6611 of the FOSTON FS-707DC reports max_page 2 in Read Local
Extended Features but answers page 2 with status 0x30, which aborted the
controller setup. Pages above 1 hold features of later Bluetooth versions:
stop reading there instead.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4456,8 +4456,18 @@
 	for (page = 2; page < HCI_MAX_PAGES && page <= hdev->max_page;
 	     page++) {
 		err = hci_read_local_ext_features_sync(hdev, page);
-		if (err)
-			return err;
+		if (err) {
+			/* The MediaTek MT6611 (Bluetooth 2.1) reports max_page 2
+			 * but rejects page 2 with "parameter out of range"
+			 * (0x30): pages above 1 only hold features of later
+			 * Bluetooth versions, so stop reading instead of
+			 * failing the whole controller setup.
+			 */
+			bt_dev_warn(hdev, "ext features page %u failed (%d), ignored",
+				    page, err);
+			hdev->max_page = page - 1;
+			break;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
